fathom — clean-room Rust port of REA (2026-10-10)
====================================================

The code in this repository is original work of Qompass AI. It is a
spec-led reimplementation of the REA reverse-engineering agent tool
(morluto/rea, MIT License), written from REA's published
documentation and contracts — its MCP tool catalog and runtime
contracts, tool-design guide, error-contract schema, architecture
notes, and provider guides — and from the behavior those documents
specify. No TypeScript source from morluto/rea was copied or
transliterated. REA's design ideas (an evidence-carrying finding
model, one provider-neutral MCP catalog, admitted per-provider
semantics) are credited here and in SPEC.md as the design source,
per the MIT terms under which those documents are published.

Where this port deviates from upstream's design (stateless per-call
tools instead of a bound binary session, a batch Ghidra export
instead of a persistent bridge process), SPEC.md names the deviation
and the reason.

